I think we should introduce one more abstraction

This idea came to me while reading back through the RFCs.

RFC-0003 introduced Cognitive Elements.

RFC-0014 introduced Memory Spaces.

Storage needs something equivalent.

I propose introducing Storage Classes.

Not every object should be stored the same way.

For example:

Storage Class	Purpose	Example
Immutable	Never changes after creation	Events, observations
Versioned	New versions replace old without losing history	Facts, entities, policies
Temporal	State changes over time	Goals, plans, world state
Derived	Computed from other objects	Embeddings, graph projections, summaries
Ephemeral	Exists briefly	Working memory, active context, caches
Archive	Rarely accessed but retained	Historical conversations, old episodes
External	Stored outside the primary database	PDFs, images, videos, datasets

This is a powerful abstraction because it tells the storage engine how an object behaves, independent of the database technology.

